                </aside>
                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Which ROC handles LLP partner change in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>ROC Mumbai at Everest House processes Form 4 and Form 3 on MCA V3 portal. FEMA LLP-I/LLP-II on RBI FIRMS portal through AD banks. DPIN via DIR-3 on MCA portal. Patron's Marine Lines office adjacent to ROC Everest House for direct coordination.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What forms are needed?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Form 4 (partner change notice) + Form 3 (supplementary agreement), both within 30 days. For new designated partners: DIR-3 for DPIN before appointment. For foreign partners: additionally LLP-I/LLP-II on FIRMS portal. Patron files all within 15 days for Mumbai LLPs.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How much notice for retirement?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>If LLP Agreement specifies: follow agreement. If silent: 30 days written notice to all partners under Section 24. Send via documented means (registered post/email). After notice period, retirement is effective. Patron manages notice process for Mumbai LLPs.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the retiring partner entitled to?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Section 24(5): original contribution + accumulated profit share (after losses) as of retirement date. If agreement specifies different formula (goodwill, revaluation): that applies. Patron computes settlement and prepares full-and-final receipt for Mumbai LLPs.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can a foreign national be a partner?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. No citizenship restriction for regular partner. But: LLP must be in 100% FDI automatic route sectors, contribution through banking channels at fair value, LLP-I within 30 days, at least 1 DP must remain Indian resident. Patron manages FEMA compliance for Mumbai LLPs.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What if LLP falls below 2 partners?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>If fewer than 2 for more than 6 months: sole partner becomes personally liable. ROC may initiate winding up. 6-month window to admit new partner. Patron advises simultaneous retirement-and-admission to prevent breach for Mumbai LLPs.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Must a designated partner be Indian resident?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>At least 1 of minimum 2 DPs must be Indian resident (182+ days in preceding FY). All DPs need DPIN via DIR-3. If only resident DP exits: replacement resident DP appointed simultaneously. Patron monitors DP residency status for Mumbai LLPs.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the late filing penalty?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Rs 100/day per form, NO cap. Form 4 + Form 3 both within 30 days. Both delayed 6 months = Rs 36,000. Non-compliance blocks annual filings and marks LLP as defaulting. Patron files within 15 days to prevent all penalties for Mumbai LLPs.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>LLP mein naya partner kaise add kare?</strong> Sab partners ki consent lo. Naya partner ka DPIN lo agar DP banana hai (DIR-3). Supplementary deed stamp paper pe &ndash; contribution, profit share, role. Form 4 + Form 3 file karo 30 din mein. Foreign partner toh LLP-I bhi. Patron 15 din mein file karta hai.</p>
                <p><strong>Partner retire ho raha hai?</strong> Agreement check karo notice period. Silent hai toh 30 din ka notice. Settlement: original contribution + accumulated profit share (Section 24(5)). Deed banao. Form 4 + Form 3 file karo. Patron settlement + filing sab manage karta hai.</p>
                <p><strong>Designated partner change?</strong> Naye DP ka DPIN hona chahiye (DIR-3). Minimum 2 DPs (1 Indian resident). Resolution pass karo. Form 4 + Form 3 file karo. Patron DPIN se filing tak sab manage karta hai.</p>

